PARITY (web LiveStaleDataBanner.tsx -> native)
  Data sources (P1/S8 state-holder seam, no HTTP in the view):
    useLiveConnection() -> LiveStaleDataBannerSource emits LiveStaleDataBannerInput (the live status the hook
                          reports: connected/reconnecting/disconnected/unknown, plus when it was entered —
                          the peer of the hook's `stateEnteredAtRef` / the banner's `disconnectedSinceRef` —
                          and the reading's freshness). The view never reads the SSE transport directly. The
                          companion `LiveIndicator` surface models the same four-state taxonomy.
    useTranslation       -> LiveStaleDataBannerStrings P1/S10 facade (every literal keyed).
  Threshold: web `STALE_BANNER_THRESHOLD_MS = 2 * 60_000` -> LiveStaleWindow.threshold = 120s. The banner shows
             only when `status === 'disconnected'` has persisted >= 120s (the web sustained-outage guard that
             avoids flapping on transient reconnects); a main-run-loop ticker re-derives the state so the
             promotion needs no further transport traffic (the web one-shot `setTimeout`).
  Render guard: web `if (!show) return null` (every non-disconnected status, and a sub-2-min disconnect) ->
                the friendly `healthy` empty leaf (never a blank box; P4 leaf contract). Disclosed native
                choice: native uses the source-provided status-entry time (truer than the web's mount-time
                ref), so a page opened mid-outage shows the banner immediately rather than restarting the timer.
  Composition: warning-toned alert banner (web `variant="warning"` -> statusWarning) + the wifi-slash glyph
               (web `<WifiOff/>`), the "Live data unavailable" title, and the two-minute reassurance body
               (web `t('live.staleBanner.message', …)`), plus a P4 connection chip (Offline / Stale) with a
               tap-to-reconnect affordance and a one-shot auto re-subscribe on the stale transition.
  i18n keys (web -> catalog, BOTH reproduced — no scope narrowing): live.staleBanner.title, live.staleBanner.message
               (the only two `t()` calls the web component makes) — both present; + P4 leaf chrome + chip keys.
  States rendered (every one, no hidden surface): loading (unknown), healthy (connected/reconnecting/sub-2-min
               disconnect -> web null), stale (the warning banner = the surface's offline/stale data state),
               error (native leaf with retry). The web "offline" and "stale" are the SAME physical condition
               for this surface (its own message says "offline for more than 2 minutes … values may be stale");
               both render via the banner + the Offline/Stale chip.

